      "label": "Distinct signals and an expertise association",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "page": 1,
          "text": "At the group level, results showed \nthat manipulations of form resulted in P600 effects, with syntactically invalid code generating more \npositive deflections in the 500–800 ms range than syntactically valid code. Meaning manipulations \nresulted in N400 effects, with semantically implausible code generating more negative deflections in \nthe 300–500 ms range than semantically plausible code. Greater Python expertise within the group \nwas associated with greater sensitivity to violations in form.",
